    "narration": "*Nicco takes in the spread of the square — the churned earth, the holding pens, the clerks at their papers, a caravan being unloaded near the far edge. The auction crowd presses closest around the display area, where a handler holds a captive still while bids volley back and forth.*\n\n*The nearest vendor is a compact man with large, damaged hands and a hooked nose, standing beside a low table strewn with ledgers and binding cord. His small, mobile eyes track Nicco's glance and the polite nod. He gives a brief nod back, unhurried, and lets his gaze settle on Nicco with the patient attention of someone who has learned to wait for the buyer to speak first.*",
