    "narration": "*The square stretches wide under overcast sky, packed earth trodden into uneven ruts where wagon wheels have cut their paths. Buyers drift between the auction area and the row of licensed sellers behind it, some leading purchases away by rope or collar, others still weighing their options. A handler near the pens calls out a number, and a clerk scratches something into a ledger without looking up.*\n\n*The nearest vendor — a short, compact man with large, rough-knuckled hands and a hooked nose — stands beside a wooden platform where three people sit on the ground, wrists bound. His small, quick eyes track Nicco's gaze across the display, then back to his face. He lifts his chin slightly at the nod, acknowledging it without enthusiasm, and lets a beat pass before speaking.*\n\nLooking for anything particular, or just browsing?\n\n*His tone is flat and practiced, the question of a man who has asked it a thousand times and expects no interesting answer. Behind him, one of the seated figures — a young woman with mud on her knees and hollow, unfocused eyes — does not look up.*",
